"Excel delivers all numbers as floats in the interactive mode, which is the "
"reason why the `int` converter rounds numbers first before turning them into "
"integers. Otherwise it could happen that e.g., 5 might be returned as 4 in "
"case it is represented as a floating point number that is slightly smaller "
"than 5. Should you require Python's original `int` in your converter, use "
"raw int` instead."
